{"zh":[{"start":4.31,"end":8.54,"text":"NASA 天体物理"},{"start":10.99,"end":15.57,"text":"旁白：海山二是一万光年以内质量最大的恒星。"},{"start":16.48,"end":19.53,"text":"十九世纪中叶，一次剧烈的爆发"},{"start":19.57,"end":23.45,"text":"把足以组成至少十个太阳的气体抛向太空，"},{"start":23.5,"end":26.53,"text":"形成了一个至今仍可见的膨胀星云。"},{"start":26.75,"end":30.27,"text":"NASA 卫星、地面望远镜"},{"start":30.29,"end":33.18,"text":"和理论模型的新成果，正在让天文学家"},{"start":33.2,"end":35.77,"text":"更好地理解这个系统。"},{"start":35.83,"end":38.93,"text":"星云的中心是两颗巨星。"},{"start":39.2,"end":42.19,"text":"两颗中较小的那颗质量是太阳的 30 倍，"},{"start":42.23,"end":44.09,"text":"亮度是太阳的一百万倍。"},{"start":44.25,"end":48.98,"text":"主星重达 90 个太阳，亮度是伴星的 5 倍。"},{"start":49.24,"end":53.28,"text":"两颗星都会产生强大的外流，叫做恒星风，"},{"start":53.3,"end":55.08,"text":"但主星的星风非常稠密，"},{"start":55.09,"end":58.25,"text":"挡住了天文学家对这颗星的直接观测。"},{"start":59.06,"end":62.27,"text":"伴星的轨道是已知最扁的轨道之一。"},{"start":62.49,"end":64.14,"text":"每隔五年半，"},{"start":64.18,"end":67.79,"text":"当两颗星摆向最近点，也就是近星点时，"},{"start":67.82,"end":70.94,"text":"它们彼此的距离差不多和火星到太阳一样近。"},{"start":72.03,"end":76.23,"text":"海山二最近一次近星点在 2014 年 8 月，"},{"start":76.27,"end":79.05,"text":"NASA 的许多太空望远镜"},{"start":79.09,"end":82.03,"text":"以及地面天文台都在观看。"},{"start":82.81,"end":84.45,"text":"在恒星风相撞的地方，"},{"start":84.49,"end":87.02,"text":"温度高达数亿度——"},{"start":87.07,"end":89.2,"text":"热到足以发出 X 射线。"},{"start":89.44,"end":92.54,"text":"但 X 射线辐射在近星点附近会消失，"},{"start":92.56,"end":96.7,"text":"因为较小的星被它大伴星的稠密星风吞没了。"},{"start":97.8,"end":101.02,"text":"过了近星点，X 射线会逐渐恢复，"},{"start":101.04,"end":103.45,"text":"但每次恢复的方式都略有不同，"},{"start":103.51,"end":106.53,"text":"说明相互较量的星风结构有变化。"},{"start":107.08,"end":111.89,"text":"最近的观测帮理论学家改进了这种相互作用的计算机模型。"},{"start":112.22,"end":116.73,"text":"这里，颜色越深表示恒星周围的气体越稀薄，"},{"start":116.78,"end":119.86,"text":"而恒星本身显示为黑色圆圈。"},{"start":120.01,"end":123.17,"text":"两颗星相距较远时，星风正面相撞，"},{"start":123.21,"end":127.01,"text":"形成一个巨大的空腔，周围是五千万度的气体。"},{"start":127.2,"end":131.08,"text":"但在近星点附近，伴星绕着大星急转，"},{"start":131.13,"end":133.66,"text":"在主星的稠密星风中凿出一条隧道。"},{"start":133.93,"end":138.98,"text":"伴星的快速运动让碰撞区从头部……转到尾部。"},{"start":139.67,"end":143.47,"text":"较小那颗星更快的星风沿着它造出的空腔流出，"},{"start":143.52,"end":146.76,"text":"然后撞上伴星向外运动的星风。"},{"start":147.81,"end":150.78,"text":"从我们在地球上的角度看，X 射线先变暗，"},{"start":150.8,"end":153.13,"text":"随着两颗星远离，又恢复过来。"},{"start":153.82,"end":156.55,"text":"这些模拟的新 3D 模型显示，"},{"start":156.56,"end":160.97,"text":"在近星点附近，空腔边缘形成了手指状的突起，"},{"start":161.0,"end":163.1,"text":"这是以前从未发现过的特征。"},{"start":163.48,"end":168.21,"text":"正在研究这一现象的理论学家认为，它们可能源于"},{"start":168.25,"end":171.34,"text":"气体沿空腔壁流动时形成的不稳定性。"},{"start":172.21,"end":174.68,"text":"天文学家还用哈勃太空望远镜"},{"start":174.71,"end":176.57,"text":"盯着海山二。"},{"start":177.53,"end":180.19,"text":"这些图像显示了一个像螃蟹的结构，"},{"start":180.22,"end":184.3,"text":"由被伴星强烈紫外光激发的气体形成。"},{"start":185.04,"end":187.24,"text":"这道光在近星点附近会变暗，"},{"start":187.27,"end":190.74,"text":"那时伴星正穿过主星星风最稠密的部分。"},{"start":190.77,"end":194.06,"text":"气体松弛下来，回到较低的能量状态。"},{"start":195.01,"end":198.47,"text":"结果，这只“螃蟹”会出现在另一条谱线上，"},{"start":198.52,"end":201.69,"text":"直到两颗星分开、紫外光恢复。"},{"start":203.05,"end":207.41,"text":"海山二是离我们最近、质量最大的星风碰撞双星之一，"},{"start":207.48,"end":209.5,"text":"是一座天然实验室，"},{"start":209.53,"end":212.11,"text":"可以研究这类罕见而重要的天体。"},{"start":212.9,"end":215.53,"text":"虽然它过去的爆发仍无法解释，"},{"start":215.59,"end":218.5,"text":"天文学家认为他们已经掌握了它目前的状态——"},{"start":218.53,"end":223.0,"text":"这个说法将在 2020 年 2 月的下一次近星点接受检验。"}],"de":[],"en":[{"start":4.31,"end":8.54,"text":"NASA ASTROPHYSICS","words":[["NASA","NASA"],["ASTROPHYSICS","天体物理"]]},{"start":10.99,"end":15.57,"text":"Narrator: Eta Carinae is the most massive star within 10,000 light-years.","words":[["Narrator:","旁白："],["Eta","海山"],["Carinae","二"],["is","是"],["the","这"],["most","最"],["massive","大质量"],["star","恒星"],["within","在"],["10,000","一万"],["light-years.","光年。"]]},{"start":16.48,"end":19.53,"text":"In the mid-nineteenth century, a tremendous eruption","words":[["In","在"],["the","这"],["mid-nineteenth","十九世纪"],["century,","中叶，"],["a","一次"],["tremendous","剧烈的"],["eruption","爆发"]]},{"start":19.57,"end":23.45,"text":"hurled enough gas into space to make at least 10 copies of the sun,","words":[["hurled","抛出"],["enough","足够"],["gas","气体"],["into","进"],["space","太空"],["to","去"],["make","组成"],["at","在"],["least","至少"],["10","10"],["copies","份"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["sun,","太阳，"]]},{"start":23.5,"end":26.53,"text":"creating an expanding nebula still visible today.","words":[["creating","形成"],["an","一个"],["expanding","膨胀的"],["nebula","星云"],["still","仍"],["visible","可见"],["today.","今天。"]]},{"start":26.75,"end":30.27,"text":"New results from NASA satellites, ground-based telescopes,","words":[["New","新的"],["results","结果"],["from","来自"],["NASA","NASA"],["satellites,","卫星，"],["ground-based","地面"],["telescopes,","望远镜，"]]},{"start":30.29,"end":33.18,"text":"and theoretical models are providing astronomers","words":[["and","和"],["theoretical","理论"],["models","模型"],["are","正在"],["providing","提供"],["astronomers","天文学家"]]},{"start":33.2,"end":35.77,"text":"with an improved understanding of the system.","words":[["with","以"],["an","一个"],["improved","更好的"],["understanding","理解"],["of","对"],["the","这"],["system.","系统。"]]},{"start":35.83,"end":38.93,"text":"At the nebula's heart lie two giant stars.","words":[["At","在"],["the","这"],["nebula's","星云的"],["heart","中心"],["lie","存在"],["two","两颗"],["giant","巨大"],["stars.","星。"]]},{"start":39.2,"end":42.19,"text":"The smaller of the two is 30 times the mass of the sun","words":[["The","这"],["smaller","较小"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["two","两颗"],["is","是"],["30","30"],["times","倍"],["the","这"],["mass","质量"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["sun","太阳"]]},{"start":42.23,"end":44.09,"text":"and a million times brighter.","words":[["and","和"],["a","一"],["million","百万"],["times","倍"],["brighter.","更亮。"]]},{"start":44.25,"end":48.98,"text":"The primary weighs 90 suns and shines 5 times brighter than its companion.","words":[["The","这"],["primary","主星"],["weighs","重"],["90","90"],["suns","太阳"],["and","和"],["shines","发光"],["5","5"],["times","倍"],["brighter","更亮"],["than","比"],["its","它的"],["companion.","伴星。"]]},{"start":49.24,"end":53.28,"text":"Both stars produce powerful outflows called stellar winds,","words":[["Both","两颗"],["stars","星"],["produce","产生"],["powerful","强大的"],["outflows","外流"],["called","叫做"],["stellar","恒星"],["winds,","风，"]]},{"start":53.3,"end":55.08,"text":"but the primary's is so dense","words":[["but","但"],["the","这"],["primary's","主星的"],["is","是"],["so","如此"],["dense","稠密"]]},{"start":55.09,"end":58.25,"text":"it prevents astronomers from directly observing the star.","words":[["it","它"],["prevents","阻止"],["astronomers","天文学家"],["from","从"],["directly","直接"],["observing","观测"],["the","这"],["star.","星。"]]},{"start":59.06,"end":62.27,"text":"The secondary's orbit is among the most eccentric known.","words":[["The","这"],["secondary's","伴星的"],["orbit","轨道"],["is","是"],["among","之一"],["the","这"],["most","最"],["eccentric","偏心的"],["known.","已知。"]]},{"start":62.49,"end":64.14,"text":"Every five and a half years,","words":[["Every","每"],["five","五"],["and","和"],["a","一"],["half","半"],["years,","年，"]]},{"start":64.18,"end":67.79,"text":"when the two stars swing toward closest approach, or periastron,","words":[["when","当"],["the","这"],["two","两颗"],["stars","星"],["swing","摆"],["toward","向"],["closest","最近"],["approach,","接近，"],["or","或"],["periastron,","近星点，"]]},{"start":67.82,"end":70.94,"text":"the come about as close to each other as Mars is from the sun.","words":[["the","它们"],["come","来到"],["about","大约"],["as","一样"],["close","近"],["to","对"],["each","彼此"],["other","之间"],["as","如同"],["Mars","火星"],["is","是"],["from","离"],["the","这"],["sun.","太阳。"]]},{"start":72.03,"end":76.23,"text":"Eta Carinae's most recent periastron occurred in August 2014,","words":[["Eta","海山"],["Carinae's","二的"],["most","最"],["recent","近的"],["periastron","近星点"],["occurred","发生"],["in","在"],["August","八月"],["2014,","2014，"]]},{"start":76.27,"end":79.05,"text":"and many of NASA's space-based telescopes,","words":[["and","和"],["many","许多"],["of","的"],["NASA's","NASA的"],["space-based","太空"],["telescopes,","望远镜，"]]},{"start":79.09,"end":82.03,"text":"as well as ground-based observatories, looked on.","words":[["as","以及"],["well","还"],["as","有"],["ground-based","地面"],["observatories,","天文台，"],["looked","观看"],["on.","着。"]]},{"start":82.81,"end":84.45,"text":"Where the stellar winds collide,","words":[["Where","在"],["the","这"],["stellar","恒星"],["winds","风"],["collide,","相撞，"]]},{"start":84.49,"end":87.02,"text":"temperatures reach hundreds of millions degrees -","words":[["temperatures","温度"],["reach","达到"],["hundreds","数百"],["of","的"],["millions","百万"],["degrees","度"],["-","-"]]},{"start":87.07,"end":89.2,"text":"hot enough to emit X-rays.","words":[["hot","热"],["enough","足以"],["to","发出"],["emit","X"],["X-rays.","射线。"]]},{"start":89.44,"end":92.54,"text":"But the X-ray emission shuts down near periastron,","words":[["But","但"],["the","这"],["X-ray","X射线"],["emission","辐射"],["shuts","关闭"],["down","掉"],["near","附近"],["periastron,","近星点，"]]},{"start":92.56,"end":96.7,"text":"when the smaller star is swallowed up by the dense wind of its larger companion.","words":[["when","当"],["the","这"],["smaller","较小"],["star","星"],["is","是"],["swallowed","吞"],["up","没"],["by","由"],["the","这"],["dense","稠密"],["wind","风"],["of","的"],["its","它的"],["larger","较大"],["companion.","伴星。"]]},{"start":97.8,"end":101.02,"text":"The X-rays gradually recover after periastron,","words":[["The","这"],["X-rays","X射线"],["gradually","逐渐"],["recover","恢复"],["after","之后"],["periastron,","近星点，"]]},{"start":101.04,"end":103.45,"text":"but they do so a bit differently each time,","words":[["but","但"],["they","它们"],["do","做"],["so","如此"],["a","一"],["bit","点"],["differently","不同地"],["each","每"],["time,","次，"]]},{"start":103.51,"end":106.53,"text":"suggesting structural changes in the dueling winds.","words":[["suggesting","表明"],["structural","结构"],["changes","变化"],["in","在"],["the","这"],["dueling","较量的"],["winds.","风。"]]},{"start":107.08,"end":111.89,"text":"Recent observations have helped theorists refine computer models of this interaction.","words":[["Recent","最近的"],["observations","观测"],["have","已经"],["helped","帮助"],["theorists","理论家"],["refine","改进"],["computer","计算机"],["models","模型"],["of","的"],["this","这"],["interaction.","相互作用。"]]},{"start":112.22,"end":116.73,"text":"Here, darker colors indicate lower gas densities around the stars,","words":[["Here,","这里，"],["darker","更深的"],["colors","颜色"],["indicate","表示"],["lower","更低的"],["gas","气体"],["densities","密度"],["around","周围"],["the","这"],["stars,","星，"]]},{"start":116.78,"end":119.86,"text":"while the stars themselves appear as black circles.","words":[["while","而"],["the","这"],["stars","星"],["themselves","本身"],["appear","显示"],["as","为"],["black","黑色"],["circles.","圆圈。"]]},{"start":120.01,"end":123.17,"text":"When the stars are far apart, the winds collide head-on,","words":[["When","当"],["the","这"],["stars","星"],["are","是"],["far","远"],["apart,","分开，"],["the","这"],["winds","风"],["collide","相撞"],["head-on,","正面，"]]},{"start":123.21,"end":127.01,"text":"creating a huge cavity surrounded by 50-million-degree gas.","words":[["creating","形成"],["a","一个"],["huge","巨大的"],["cavity","空腔"],["surrounded","包围"],["by","由"],["50-million-degree","五千万度"],["gas.","气体。"]]},{"start":127.2,"end":131.08,"text":"But near periastron, the secondary whips around the larger star,","words":[["But","但"],["near","附近"],["periastron,","近星点，"],["the","这"],["secondary","伴星"],["whips","急转"],["around","绕"],["the","这"],["larger","较大"],["star,","星，"]]},{"start":131.13,"end":133.66,"text":"carving a tunnel though the primary's dense wind.","words":[["carving","凿出"],["a","一条"],["tunnel","隧道"],["though","穿过"],["the","这"],["primary's","主星的"],["dense","稠密"],["wind.","风。"]]},{"start":133.93,"end":138.98,"text":"The secondary star's rapid motion changes the collision zone from head... to tail.","words":[["The","这"],["secondary","伴星"],["star's","星的"],["rapid","快速"],["motion","运动"],["changes","改变"],["the","这"],["collision","碰撞"],["zone","区"],["from","从"],["head...","头……"],["to","到"],["tail.","尾。"]]},{"start":139.67,"end":143.47,"text":"The smaller star's faster wind flows out along the cavity it created","words":[["The","这"],["smaller","较小"],["star's","星的"],["faster","更快"],["wind","风"],["flows","流"],["out","出"],["along","沿着"],["the","这"],["cavity","空腔"],["it","它"],["created","造出"]]},{"start":143.52,"end":146.76,"text":"and then crashes into the outward-moving wind of its companion.","words":[["and","然后"],["then","撞"],["crashes","进"],["into","这"],["the","向外"],["outward-moving","运动的"],["wind","风"],["of","的"],["its","它的"],["companion.","伴星。"]]},{"start":147.81,"end":150.78,"text":"From out perspective on Earth, the X-rays fade,","words":[["From","从"],["out","我们的"],["perspective","角度"],["on","在"],["Earth,","地球，"],["the","这"],["X-rays","X射线"],["fade,","变暗，"]]},{"start":150.8,"end":153.13,"text":"then recover, as the stars move apart.","words":[["then","然后"],["recover,","恢复，"],["as","随着"],["the","这"],["stars","星"],["move","移"],["apart.","开。"]]},{"start":153.82,"end":156.55,"text":"New 3D models of these simulations reveal","words":[["New","新"],["3D","3D"],["models","模型"],["of","的"],["these","这些"],["simulations","模拟"],["reveal","显示"]]},{"start":156.56,"end":160.97,"text":"the formation of finger-like protrusions along the cavity near periastron,","words":[["the","这"],["formation","形成"],["of","的"],["finger-like","手指状"],["protrusions","突起"],["along","沿着"],["the","这"],["cavity","空腔"],["near","附近"],["periastron,","近星点，"]]},{"start":161.0,"end":163.1,"text":"features never before identified.","words":[["features","特征"],["never","从未"],["before","以前"],["identified.","发现。"]]},{"start":163.48,"end":168.21,"text":"Theorists now investigating the phenomenon suggest they may arise from instabilities","words":[["Theorists","理论家"],["now","现在"],["investigating","研究"],["the","这"],["phenomenon","现象"],["suggest","认为"],["they","它们"],["may","可能"],["arise","产生"],["from","源于"],["instabilities","不稳定性"]]},{"start":168.25,"end":171.34,"text":"developing in gas as it flows along the cavity wall.","words":[["developing","形成"],["in","在"],["gas","气体"],["as","当"],["it","它"],["flows","流"],["along","沿着"],["the","这"],["cavity","空腔"],["wall.","壁。"]]},{"start":172.21,"end":174.68,"text":"Astronomers also keep an eye on Eta Carinae","words":[["Astronomers","天文学家"],["also","也"],["keep","保持"],["an","一"],["eye","眼"],["on","在"],["Eta","海山"],["Carinae","二"]]},{"start":174.71,"end":176.57,"text":"with the Hubble Space Telescope.","words":[["with","用"],["the","这"],["Hubble","哈勃"],["Space","太空"],["Telescope.","望远镜。"]]},{"start":177.53,"end":180.19,"text":"These images show a structure resembling a crab,","words":[["These","这些"],["images","图像"],["show","显示"],["a","一个"],["structure","结构"],["resembling","像"],["a","一只"],["crab,","螃蟹，"]]},{"start":180.22,"end":184.3,"text":"formed by gas excited by the secondary star's intense UV light.","words":[["formed","形成"],["by","由"],["gas","气体"],["excited","激发"],["by","由"],["the","这"],["secondary","伴星"],["star's","星的"],["intense","强烈"],["UV","紫外"],["light.","光。"]]},{"start":185.04,"end":187.24,"text":"This light dims near periastron,","words":[["This","这"],["light","光"],["dims","变暗"],["near","近"],["periastron,","近星点，"]]},{"start":187.27,"end":190.74,"text":"when the secondary passes through the thickest part of the primary's wind.","words":[["when","当"],["the","这"],["secondary","伴星"],["passes","穿"],["through","过"],["the","这"],["thickest","最厚"],["part","部分"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["primary's","主星的"],["wind.","风。"]]},{"start":190.77,"end":194.06,"text":"The gas relaxes, settling into a lower-energy state.","words":[["The","这"],["gas","气体"],["relaxes,","松弛，"],["settling","回到"],["into","进"],["a","一个"],["lower-energy","低能量"],["state.","状态。"]]},{"start":195.01,"end":198.47,"text":"As a result, the crab appears in a different spectral line","words":[["As","作为"],["a","一个"],["result,","结果，"],["the","这"],["crab","螃蟹"],["appears","出现"],["in","在"],["a","一条"],["different","不同的"],["spectral","光谱"],["line","线"]]},{"start":198.52,"end":201.69,"text":"until the stars move apart and the UV light is restored.","words":[["until","直到"],["the","这"],["stars","星"],["move","移"],["apart","开"],["and","和"],["the","这"],["UV","紫外"],["light","光"],["is","是"],["restored.","恢复。"]]},{"start":203.05,"end":207.41,"text":"Eta Carinae is one of the closest and most massive colliding-wind binaries,","words":[["Eta","海山"],["Carinae","二"],["is","是"],["one","之一"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["closest","最近"],["and","和"],["most","最"],["massive","大质量"],["colliding-wind","星风碰撞"],["binaries,","双星，"]]},{"start":207.48,"end":209.5,"text":"and serves as a natural laboratory","words":[["and","和"],["serves","充当"],["as","作为"],["a","一个"],["natural","天然"],["laboratory","实验室"]]},{"start":209.53,"end":212.11,"text":"for studying these rare and important objects.","words":[["for","用于"],["studying","研究"],["these","这些"],["rare","罕见"],["and","和"],["important","重要"],["objects.","天体。"]]},{"start":212.9,"end":215.53,"text":"While its past eruptions remain unexplained,","words":[["While","虽然"],["its","它的"],["past","过去"],["eruptions","爆发"],["remain","仍"],["unexplained,","无法解释，"]]},{"start":215.59,"end":218.5,"text":"astronomers think they have a handle on its current state--","words":[["astronomers","天文学家"],["think","认为"],["they","他们"],["have","有"],["a","一个"],["handle","把握"],["on","在"],["its","它的"],["current","目前"],["state--","状态——"]]},{"start":218.53,"end":223.0,"text":"a claim to be tested at the next periastron in February 2020.","words":[["a","一个"],["claim","说法"],["to","要"],["be","被"],["tested","检验"],["at","在"],["the","这"],["next","下一次"],["periastron","近星点"],["in","在"],["February","二月"],["2020.","2020。"]]}]}